m about votes cast by peers other than the one delivering the request.\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\": {\\\"wait_millis\\\": 200, \\\"applied_commands\\\": 20, \\\"peers\\\": 3, \\\"claimed_term_offset\\\": 1}\n  },\n  \\\"prefix\\\": \\\"The new case builds a three-peer cluster with MakeClusterCustom(MakeClusterOpts{Peers: 3, Bootstrap: true, CommitTrackingLogs: true, Conf: inmemConfig with TrailingLogs 10 and RestoreCommittedLogs set per case}), demotes one non-leader peer to a nonvoter, applies 20 entries so both peers hold the same log, reads the responder's own configuration entry, voter count and snapshot count, stops only the responder and emits a vote_inputs CA_EVENT, then rebuilds the responder over its own stores and reconnects it in both directions to the two live peers. It stops the leader, waits 200 ms, reads the responder's reconstructed configuration and term, and sends a RequestVoteRequest built from the demoted peer's own header, identity and last log entry with a term one above, through that peer's in-memory transport to the restarted instance. It then emits a vote_grant CA_EVENT with the responder's reconstructed voter count, its log's voter count, the granted flag, the response term, the responder's terms before and after, the candidate's membership and vote status in the committed configuration, and the vote term and candidate persisted in the responder's stable store before and after the request.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\": \\\"requestVote owns the decision to grant support, and its membership and voter gates are the only checks that bind a node's vote to the committed configuration; the reconstructed configuration is what those gates read.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\": [{\\\"alias\\\": \\\"state\\\", \\\"event\\\": \\\"vote_inputs\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshot_count\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"candidate_has_vote\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}]}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\": [\n   {\\\"event\\\": \\\"vote_grant\\\", \\\"identity_fields\\\": [\\\"scenario\\\",\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\"], \\\"admission_alias\\\": \\\"state\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\": {\\\"field\\\": \\\"granted\\\", \\\"value\\\": False},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\":\\\"scenario\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"vote_gate_after_restart\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}],\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Vote-path case with the flag enabled: a peer that holds no vote in the configuration recorded in the responder's own log is not expected to receive the responder's vote.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\": \\\"vote_grant\\\", \\\"identity_fields\\\": [\\\"scenario\\\",\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\"], \\\"admission_alias\\\": \\\"state\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\": {\\\"field\\\": \\\"granted\\\", \\\"value\\\": False},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\": [{\\\"field\\\":\\\"scenario\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"vote_gate_after_restart\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}],\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Control: with the flag disabled the same request from the same peer is refused because that peer holds no vote in the responder's configuration.\\\"}\n  ]\n }\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(sub, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_12-31-30-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"written\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"d8459ce0e23540cea18c9bc82878e37d\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 1879.383455438001, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": tr